! QCD dijet background. Flavor split (light/c/b) is done at analysis time by
! hadron-based jet labeling, so one inclusive sample serves all three ROCs.
! pTHat slice set below the 500 GeV jet cut so the cut is not sitting on the
! generator turn-on. At pTHatMin = 450 the jet spectrum peaked on the threshold
! and the selection sculpted the sample that the pT reweighting then had to
! correct. Lowering to 400 buys margin; 300 would be fully efficient but costs
! a factor ~6 in selected jets per generated event (measured).
! Random seed is set programmatically.

Beams:idA = 2212
Beams:idB = 2212
Beams:eCM = 13600.

HardQCD:all = on
PhaseSpace:pTHatMin = 400.

Random:setSeed = on
Next:numberShowEvent = 0
Next:numberShowProcess = 0
Next:numberShowInfo = 0
Print:quiet = on
